# CONSENSUS.flow

```text
╔════════════════════════════════════╗
║           CONSENSUS GATE           ║
║                                    ║
║  input:  Proposal {Thought, hash}  ║
║  state:  pending weights           ║
║                                    ║
║  OPEN when:                        ║
║    Σ weights ≥ θ                   ║
║    OR Queen.approve                ║
║                                    ║
║  CLOSED when:                      ║
║    Queen.veto                      ║
║    OR timeout                      ║
║                                    ║
║  on OPEN  → emit AUTHORIZED        ║
║  on CLOSE → emit REJECTED          ║
║                                    ║
║  The Gate holds no private key.    ║
║  The Gate only counts.             ║
╚════════════════════════════════════╝

INVARIANT:
  Authorization is a count, not a signature.
  (This is the experimental opposite of the Loom seal.)
```
